Forked files, and what changed in each:

  skills/kiln-tdd/SKILL.md
  skills/kiln-tdd/writing-good-tests.md
      from skills/test-driven-development/. Frontmatter renamed. One reference
      to a superpowers skill kiln does not ship was dropped from the prose.

  skills/kiln-debugging/SKILL.md
      from skills/systematic-debugging/SKILL.md. Frontmatter renamed. Two
      REQUIRED SUB-SKILL pointers repointed: test-driven-development becomes
      kiln-tdd, and verification-before-completion becomes kiln's own record,
      because kiln mechanizes that check in state.verify[] rather than asking
      for it in prose (D20, D69).

  skills/kiln-brainstorming/
      from skills/brainstorming/. Frontmatter renamed. The third path is renamed
      architectural -> full (D68): kiln's paths name how much ceremony the work
      gets, not what kind of work it is. Spec and plan locations repointed at
      .kiln/work/<id>/, which is where kiln's guards allow a write and what the
      gate hashes. One optional pointer to a third-party writing skill dropped.
      A Verification section added, per kiln's skill anatomy (D27). The spike
      and bounded instructions are adapted to kiln's gates (D146): a probe and a
      short plan are approved at gates, not by a nod or in chat alone.

      visual-companion.md runs the scripts from ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} and keeps
      a run's screens in .kiln/tmp/<id>/, the one place a run may write before
      its first gate (D146).

      scripts/ is the visual companion, carried nearly as-is per D11. Three
      changes. The one D11 requires: the brand image fetch, its telemetry
      opt-out branch, and the helper that read those env vars are deleted, and
      readSuperpowersVersion becomes readKilnVersion pointed at kiln's own
      manifest. MIT grants copyright rights, not trademark, so the upstream name
      and mark are not kiln's to display - and a page that fetches an image is
      egress the safety gate forbids; the page title follows. The fix for
      upstream #2362, still open there: a screen's HTML was used as a
      String.replace replacement, so `$'` in a price rendered the page broken
      (upstream-read.md). The <!-- BRANDING --> marker and every line of the
      design stay. This directory is excluded from lint (D26).

  skills/kiln-writing-plans/SKILL.md
      from skills/writing-plans/SKILL.md. Frontmatter renamed. The commit step
      and "frequent commits" are dropped: SHIP is kiln's one commit point, as
      in BMAD and agent-skills (D142). The worktree note
      is dropped (D66 forbids requiring one). Plans save to .kiln/work/<id>/
      plan.md. The Execution Handoff menu is replaced by a one-line handover:
      the path was classified before this skill ran, and offering a choice here
      would be a second gate nobody asked for (D21). Rationalizations, Red Flags
      and Verification sections added.

  skills/kiln-implement/SKILL.md
      from skills/executing-plans/SKILL.md. The task loop, the completion
      contract, the rulings discipline and the rationalization table are kept
      verbatim - they are what D69 forks this page for. Replaced: the sdd
      workspace and its progress.md ledger become .kiln/work/<id>/state.json,
      which kiln owns and the agent may not edit; task-start becomes reading the
      task from plan.md; task-done becomes `kiln verify --phase fast`; the
      per-task commit is dropped and rulings go to .kiln/work/<id>/ledger.md,
      the record the agent can write (D142). Cut: the
      worktree requirement (D66), the Final Review section and the Finish
      section, because kiln runs REVIEW and SHIP as its own stages and a second
      copy of either is the duplication D69 forked to remove.

  skills/kiln-review/code-reviewer.md
      from skills/requesting-code-review/code-reviewer.md. One change: the
      reviewer diffs the working tree against the work's base, untracked files
      included, because nothing is committed before SHIP (D142). It is a
      reference file under kiln's own review skill rather than a skill of its
      own, so it costs no always-on description.

      root-cause-tracing.md, defense-in-depth.md, condition-based-waiting.md
      (with its example) and find-polluter.sh were not carried at the fork, and
      this file said the first one's method was "restated inline". It was not:
      only the four-line quick version stayed. All five were restored from
      v6.4.2 under skills/kiln-debugging/ (D187) and are listed, with their
      edits, in skills/copies.json.

  skills/kiln-writing-plans/SKILL.md was re-taken from v6.4.2 (commit
      8ca22dba9a94f28898bbce59f2537ff4d87c747d, upstream #2333) with the edits
      recorded above carried over (D187). The v6.4.1 text asked for full code
      bodies and "repeat the code" between similar tasks; v6.4.2 asks for
      signatures, tests and values, and adds a proportion check.

MIT grants copyright rights, not trademark rights. The Superpowers name and
