Every file kiln copies from these projects opens with a kiln note (a block of
lines beginning "> **In kiln:**") and is listed in skills/copies.json with the
source, the commit it was taken at, the upstream path, whether it is verbatim,
edited or an excerpt, each edit in words, and two sha256 hashes: the upstream
file at that commit and kiln's text under the note. tests/copies.test.mjs checks
every listed copy against its hashes and fails on an unlisted one.
`node scripts/upstream.mjs report <checkouts>` says what upstream has changed
since each copy was taken.
